- name: applovin
  type: table
  desc: Functions and constants for AppLovin MAX SDK 13.6.3 on Android and iOS.

  members:

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: initialize
    type: function
    desc: "Initializes MAX asynchronously. Install the callback and apply privacy, consent-flow,
          user, logging, mute, creative-debugger, and test-device settings first. Do not load or
          show ads until `OnSdkInitializedEvent`. Calling this function with a placeholder or an
          SDK key that does not belong to the app is an integration error."
    parameters:
      - name: sdk_key
        type: string
        desc: SDK key from MAX Dashboard > Account > General > Keys.

    examples:
      - desc: |-
          ```lua
          local function on_max_event(self, name, params)
              if name == "OnSdkInitializedEvent" then
                  applovin.load_interstitial("YOUR_AD_UNIT_ID")
              end
          end

          function init(self)
              applovin.set_callback(on_max_event)
              applovin.set_test_device_advertising_ids({ "YOUR_IDFA_OR_GAID" })
              applovin.initialize("YOUR_SDK_KEY")
          end
          ```

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_callback
    type: function
    desc: "Sets the callback that receives all MAX events on the Defold update thread. Replaces any
          previously installed callback. Pass `nil` to remove it. The callback signature is
          `function(self, name, params)`. `name` is one of the events below and `params` is a table.

          Lifecycle events:
          `OnSdkInitializedEvent`, `OnCmpCompletedEvent`.

          Interstitial events:
          `OnInterstitialAdLoadedEvent`, `OnInterstitialAdLoadFailedEvent`,
          `OnInterstitialAdDisplayedEvent`, `OnInterstitialAdDisplayFailedEvent`,
          `OnInterstitialAdHiddenEvent`, `OnInterstitialAdClickedEvent`,
          `OnInterstitialAdRevenuePaidEvent`.

          Rewarded events:
          `OnRewardedAdLoadedEvent`, `OnRewardedAdLoadFailedEvent`,
          `OnRewardedAdDisplayedEvent`, `OnRewardedAdDisplayFailedEvent`,
          `OnRewardedAdHiddenEvent`, `OnRewardedAdClickedEvent`,
          `OnRewardedAdReceivedRewardEvent`, `OnRewardedAdRevenuePaidEvent`.

          Banner events:
          `OnBannerAdLoadedEvent`, `OnBannerAdLoadFailedEvent`, `OnBannerAdClickedEvent`,
          `OnBannerAdExpandedEvent`, `OnBannerAdCollapsedEvent`,
          `OnBannerAdRevenuePaidEvent`.

          MREC events:
          `OnMRecAdLoadedEvent`, `OnMRecAdLoadFailedEvent`, `OnMRecAdClickedEvent`,
          `OnMRecAdExpandedEvent`, `OnMRecAdCollapsedEvent`, `OnMRecAdRevenuePaidEvent`.

          `OnSdkInitializedEvent` params:
          `countryCode` (string), `consentFlowUserGeography` (number),
          `isTestModeEnabled` (boolean), and `appTrackingStatus` (number, iOS only).

          `OnCmpCompletedEvent` has an empty params table on success. On failure it contains `code`
          (number), `message` (string), `cmpCode` (number), and `cmpMessage` (string).

          Successful ad, display, click, hide, expand, collapse, reward, and revenue events include
          ad information: `adUnitIdentifier`, `format`, `networkName`, `networkPlacement`,
          `creativeIdentifier`, `placement`, `revenue`, `revenuePrecision`,
          `requestLatencyMillis`, `dspName`, and `dspIdentifier`. Values unavailable from a mediated
          network may be empty or absent. Revenue is in USD and may be `0`; use
          `revenuePrecision` before interpreting it.

          `OnRewardedAdReceivedRewardEvent` additionally includes `label` (string) and `amount`
          (number).

          Load failures include `adUnitIdentifier`, `code`, `message`, and
          `requestLatencyMillis`. Display failures include available ad information plus `code`,
          `message`, `mediatedNetworkErrorCode`, and `mediatedNetworkErrorMessage`; their
          `requestLatencyMillis` is the ad request latency. Error codes and messages come from MAX
          and, for display failures, the mediated network."
    parameters:
      - name: callback
        type: function
        optional: true
        desc: Event callback, or `nil` to remove the callback.
        parameters:
          - name: self
            type: object
            desc: Script instance that installed the callback.
          - name: name
            type: string
            desc: Event name.
          - name: params
            type: table
            desc: Event payload.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_initialized
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether asynchronous SDK initialization has completed.
    returns:
      - name: initialized
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_mediation_debugger
    type: function
    desc: Shows the MAX Mediation Debugger. Use this only after SDK initialization and from a user action.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_has_user_consent
    type: function
    desc: "Sets the user's legally obtained consent state for interest-based advertising. Apply the
          value before `initialize()`. This API does not collect consent."
    parameters:
      - name: has_user_consent
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: has_user_consent
    type: function
    desc: "Returns the current user-consent value. The API cannot distinguish an explicit `false`
          from a value your application never set, so persist and apply your consent decision."
    returns:
      - name: has_user_consent
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_do_not_sell
    type: function
    desc: "Sets whether the user opted out of sale or sharing of personal information. Apply the
          legally obtained value before `initialize()`."
    parameters:
      - name: do_not_sell
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_do_not_sell
    type: function
    desc: "Returns the current do-not-sell value. The API cannot distinguish an explicit `false`
          from a value your application never set."
    returns:
      - name: do_not_sell
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_terms_and_privacy_policy_flow_enabled
    type: function
    desc: "Enables or disables MAX's Terms and Privacy Policy Flow. Configure the required CMP
          dependencies, dashboard message, privacy-policy URL, and iOS/Android app metadata first.
          Set this before `initialize()`."
    parameters:
      - name: enabled
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_privacy_policy_url
    type: function
    desc: Sets the public HTTPS privacy-policy URL used by the MAX consent flow before initialization.
    parameters:
      - name: url
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_terms_of_service_url
    type: function
    desc: Sets the optional public HTTPS Terms of Service URL used by the MAX consent flow before initialization.
    parameters:
      - name: url
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_consent_flow_debug_user_geography
    type: function
    desc: "Overrides geography for consent-flow testing. Pass `\"GDPR\"` or `\"OTHER\"`. Use only in
          development and set it before initialization."
    parameters:
      - name: geography
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_cmp_for_existing_user
    type: function
    desc: "Shows the integrated CMP for an existing user. Offer this from a privacy-settings action
          only when `has_supported_cmp()` is true; completion arrives as `OnCmpCompletedEvent`."

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: has_supported_cmp
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether a supported CMP is integrated and available.
    returns:
      - name: supported
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_tablet
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether the current device uses the SDK's tablet classification.
    returns:
      - name: tablet
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_user_id
    type: function
    desc: "Sets your internal user identifier. Do not use personally identifiable information.
          Set it before initialization when it must be available to mediated networks."
    parameters:
      - name: user_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_muted
    type: function
    desc: Requests muted audio for mediated networks that support the setting.
    parameters:
      - name: muted
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_muted
    type: function
    desc: Returns the current mute setting.
    returns:
      - name: muted
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_verbose_logging_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Enables or disables verbose MAX logging. Enable it for integration testing, not production.
    parameters:
      - name: enabled
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_verbose_logging_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Returns the current verbose-logging setting.
    returns:
      - name: enabled
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_creative_debugger_enabled
    type: function
    desc: Enables or disables the MAX Creative Debugger for QA builds.
    parameters:
      - name: enabled
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_test_device_advertising_ids
    type: function
    desc: "Sets devices that should receive test ads. Pass an array of IDFAs on iOS or GAIDs on
          Android before `initialize()`. Never ship another user's advertising identifier."
    parameters:
      - name: advertising_ids
        type: array
        desc: Array of advertising-identifier strings.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: track_event
    type: function
    desc: "Tracks a custom AppLovin event after SDK initialization with JSON string parameters.
          `event_name` must be non-empty. Invalid JSON or a non-object value is logged and sent
          as an empty parameter map."
    parameters:
      - name: event_name
        type: string
        desc: Non-empty event name.
      - name: parameters
        type: string
        desc: JSON object encoded as a string, for example `"{\"level\":\"5\"}"`.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: load_interstitial
    type: function
    desc: Starts loading an interstitial. Call only after `OnSdkInitializedEvent`.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_interstitial_ready
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether an interstitial is ready for the ad unit.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
    returns:
      - name: ready
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_interstitial
    type: function
    desc: Shows a loaded interstitial, optionally attributing it to a placement.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: placement
        type: string
        optional: true
        desc: MAX placement name.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_interstitial_extra_parameter
    type: function
    desc: Sets a MAX-supported extra parameter on an interstitial ad object.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: key
        type: string
      - name: value
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: load_rewarded_ad
    type: function
    desc: Starts loading a rewarded ad. Call only after `OnSdkInitializedEvent`.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: is_rewarded_ad_ready
    type: function
    desc: Returns whether a rewarded ad is ready for the ad unit.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
    returns:
      - name: ready
        type: boolean

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_rewarded_ad
    type: function
    desc: Shows a loaded rewarded ad, optionally attributing it to a placement.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: placement
        type: string
        optional: true
        desc: MAX placement name.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_rewarded_ad_extra_parameter
    type: function
    desc: Sets a MAX-supported extra parameter on a rewarded ad object.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: key
        type: string
      - name: value
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: create_banner
    type: function
    desc: Creates and starts loading a banner at the requested screen position.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: position
        type: string
        desc: "`top_left`, `top_center`, `top_right`, `centered`, `bottom_left`,
              `bottom_center`, or `bottom_right`."

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_banner_background_color
    type: function
    desc: Sets a banner's background color.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: hex_color
        type: string
        desc: Color in `#RRGGBB` or `#AARRGGBB` form.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_banner_placement
    type: function
    desc: "Sets the MAX placement name for a banner ad unit. Call this before `create_banner()` so
          the placement is attached to the first load; calling it later updates the existing view."
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: placement
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_banner_extra_parameter
    type: function
    desc: Sets a MAX-supported extra parameter on an existing banner.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: key
        type: string
      - name: value
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: update_banner_position
    type: function
    desc: Moves an existing banner to a supported screen position.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: position
        type: string
        desc: "`top_left`, `top_center`, `top_right`, `centered`, `bottom_left`,
              `bottom_center`, or `bottom_right`."

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: start_banner_auto_refresh
    type: function
    desc: Starts auto-refresh on an existing banner.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: stop_banner_auto_refresh
    type: function
    desc: Stops auto-refresh on an existing banner.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_banner
    type: function
    desc: Shows an existing banner.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: hide_banner
    type: function
    desc: Hides an existing banner without destroying it.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: destroy_banner
    type: function
    desc: Destroys a banner and releases its native view.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: create_mrec
    type: function
    desc: Creates and starts loading an MREC at the requested screen position.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: position
        type: string
        desc: "`top_left`, `top_center`, `top_right`, `centered`, `bottom_left`,
              `bottom_center`, or `bottom_right`."

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_mrec_placement
    type: function
    desc: "Sets the MAX placement name for an MREC ad unit. Call this before `create_mrec()` so the
          placement is attached to the first load; calling it later updates the existing view."
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: placement
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: set_mrec_extra_parameter
    type: function
    desc: Sets a MAX-supported extra parameter on an existing MREC.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: key
        type: string
      - name: value
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: update_mrec_position
    type: function
    desc: Moves an existing MREC to a supported screen position.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string
      - name: position
        type: string
        desc: "`top_left`, `top_center`, `top_right`, `centered`, `bottom_left`,
              `bottom_center`, or `bottom_right`."

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: start_mrec_auto_refresh
    type: function
    desc: Starts auto-refresh on an existing MREC.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: stop_mrec_auto_refresh
    type: function
    desc: Stops auto-refresh on an existing MREC.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: show_mrec
    type: function
    desc: Shows an existing MREC.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: hide_mrec
    type: function
    desc: Hides an existing MREC without destroying it.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: destroy_mrec
    type: function
    desc: Destroys an MREC and releases its native view.
    parameters:
      - name: ad_unit_id
        type: string

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: CONSENT_FLOW_USER_GEOGRAPHY_UNKNOWN
    type: number
    desc: Consent-flow geography is unknown.

  - name: CONSENT_FLOW_USER_GEOGRAPHY_GDPR
    type: number
    desc: User is in a GDPR-region geography.

  - name: CONSENT_FLOW_USER_GEOGRAPHY_OTHER
    type: number
    desc: User is outside the GDPR-region geography.

#*****************************************************************************************************

  - name: APP_TRACKING_TRANSPARENCY_STATUS_UNAVAILABLE
    type: number
    desc: ATT status is unavailable on this platform or OS version.

  - name: APP_TRACKING_TRANSPARENCY_STATUS_NOT_DETERMINED
    type: number
    desc: User has not yet chosen an ATT authorization state.

  - name: APP_TRACKING_TRANSPARENCY_STATUS_RESTRICTED
    type: number
    desc: Device policy restricts ATT authorization.

  - name: APP_TRACKING_TRANSPARENCY_STATUS_DENIED
    type: number
    desc: User denied ATT authorization.

  - name: APP_TRACKING_TRANSPARENCY_STATUS_AUTHORIZED
    type: number
    desc: User authorized ATT tracking access.
